 "content": "# Continual-ARC task-efce8044

Observed rule from demo and verified test: the grid contains several solid-color rectangular objects (colors vary by object, e.g. 2, 6, 7), with scattered single-cell noise/distractors in other colors. For each rectangle object, preserve its color and expand/fill it to the full axis-aligned bounding box of its same-color component; remove the stray noise cells by replacing them with background. Keep grid dimensions/background unchanged. In the demo, this filled small missing corners/cells and removed isolated color-5 specks. In the solved test, objects were rectangular blocks of 2 and 6 on background 1; isolated values such as 3,4,5,7,8,9 were noise and were replaced by background. The complete output was accepted correct.

Practical approach: locate connected large regions by their dominant colors, infer each object's bounding rectangle from its occupied rows/columns, fill all cells in that rectangle, and reset isolated outlier pixels to background. Avoid treating every non-background cell as meaningful."
